.pdxdoc-version 1
.tool           postui
.kind           library
.version        1.0.0
.author         paideia-os-team
.wave           postui-v1
.toolchain      paideia-as v0.34+
.license        MIT
.summary        Ratatui-parity TUI widget library for paideia-os
                — stack-of-widgets over a Buffer, flushed to a
                KIND_TUI_CANVAS cap, with every draw() also
                emitting a frozen-schema semantic-pipe record.

.section NAME
postui — Ratatui-parity TUI widget library for paideia-os.

.section OVERVIEW
postui is the paideia-os TUI widget library. Every `.pdx` ring-3
tool that draws a multi-pane interactive screen (`postui-top`,
`postui-hex`, `postui-dmesg`, plus every future TUI app the org
ships) links against postui rather than hand-rolling ANSI. The
model is Ratatui's immediate-mode substrate re-expressed in
`.pdx`'s primitives (closed enums + `match` dispatch, no
generics, no trait objects): the caller stacks `WidgetKind`
values against `Rect` slots each frame, `widget_draw` writes
cells into a `Buffer`, `Frame::present` diffs against the front
buffer, and the changed cells flush through a `KIND_TUI_CANVAS`
capability to `KIND_TTY`. Every `draw()` call does one more
thing: it emits a frozen-schema `*View@0.1` semantic-pipe record
alongside the cells, so a scraper or agent subscribes to what
the widget is showing without parsing the terminal stream.

.section MODULES
Every source file lands one module. All modules follow paideia-as
conformance (PascalCase basename, `cmp reg, imm32`, r11 scratch,
`xor rax, rax; mov_b rax, [ptr]` byte loads, SysV push/pop parity).

  Lib                  Library-identity constants
                       (POSTUI_VERSION_{MAJOR,MINOR,PATCH},
                       POSTUI_ERR_BAND_BASE, POSTUI_OK). No I/O,
                       no bodies — the anchor every consumer
                       compile-time checks against.
  Rect                 4×u16 geometry (x, y, rows, cols) — the
                       area passed to every draw call and every
                       layout split.
  Style               Style aggregate (fg Color, bg Color,
                       modifier bitset: bold/italic/underline/
                       inverse/…). Every Cell carries one.
  Color                24-bit truecolor triplet (r, g, b). No
                       palette / indexed / xterm-256 modes at
                       v1; the KIND_TUI_CANVAS wire is truecolor
                       throughout.
  Cell                 16-byte wire-format cell (glyph +
                       Style + width class). Buffer is a
                       row-major array of these.
  Buffer               Back/front region layout, dirty-rectangle
                       accounting, cell-by-cell diff feeding
                       TCC_OP_PRESENT.
  TuiCanvasClient      KIND_TUI_CANVAS wrappers: mint, present,
                       query_rows/cols/id/tty_id, resize, clear,
                       debug_print. Kernel band 0xFFFFEB10..1F.
  Frame                Per-frame driver: bind canvas cap, expose
                       the back buffer to widget_draw, flush
                       through TCC_OP_PRESENT at frame close.
  Block                Border + title + padding container
                       (plain/rounded/double/thick borders); the
                       one widget every other widget nests
                       inside for chrome.
  WidgetKind           Closed enum of every widget (WK_BLOCK=0 …
                       WK_CLEAR=14, WK_COUNT=15) + `widget_draw`
                       op-dispatch. Adding a widget = adding one
                       ordinal + one branch, no trait plumbing.
  Layout               Integer-only constraint splitter:
                       Length/Percentage/Ratio/Min/Max/Fill,
                       largest-remainder (Hamilton) apportionment,
                       clamp-and-redistribute, totally
                       deterministic (§2.4 of the design).
  Text                 Span (styled UTF-8 run) + Line (span list)
                       + Text (line list) + wrap/trunc helpers.
                       The unit every text-bearing widget consumes.
  Width                UTF-8 byte scan + East-Asian-Width table
                       for column-width calculation. Stdlib
                       routine, not a compiler gap.
  SemanticRegistry     Per-widget schema-hash constants
                       (SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_{BLKV,PGVW,LSVW,TBVW,
                       TABV,SBVW,…}) + `semantic_send` /
                       `semantic_binding_init` /
                       `semantic_binding_dispatch`. The
                       libpdx-semantic-pipe Send/Binding glue.
  Padding              Rect inset utility (uniform + per-edge),
                       used by Block chrome and by widgets that
                       reserve internal margins.
  Fixed64              Q32.32 signed fixed-point (paideia-as-
                       native, no float codegen). The
                       coordinate/scale type for Chart axes
                       and Canvas shapes.
  Terminal             Input dispatcher: KIND_TTY raw-mode
                       primary path (once `#1986` /
                       R66v2.POS-001 lands), sys_read(0)
                       fallback (removed at postui.M4-007).
  Event                Closed enum: Key(u32) / Resize(u16, u16) /
                       Mouse{x,y,button,mods} / Paste([u8; N]).
  EscParser            CSI/SS3/OSC ESC-sequence state machine;
                       accumulates parameter bytes across
                       partial reads and hands Event to Terminal.
  Widgets/*            One module per widget in the catalog
                       below (src/widgets/<name>.pdx).

.section WIDGET_CATALOG
Fifteen widgets ship at v1. Every widget's `draw()` writes cells
into the current Buffer AND calls `<w>_view_pack` to lay a
`<Name>View@0.1` semantic record into caller-provided memory;
`semantic_send(SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_<TAG>, rec, len)` routes it to
the app's subscriber pipe.

  Block          Border + title + padding container.
                 → BlockView@0.1        (title text, border kind)
  Paragraph      Wrapped + styled text block with scroll offset.
                 → ParagraphView@0.1    (wrapped line count, scroll)
  List           Selectable scrolling list + ListState cursor.
                 → ListView@0.1         (item_count, selected_index,
                                        viewport_offset, null-sep labels)
  Table          Column-aligned selectable rows + TableState.
                 → TableView@0.1        (row count, column headers,
                                        selected row)
  Tabs           Horizontal tab bar with a selected index.
                 → TabsView@0.1         (labels, selected_index)
  Scrollbar      Track + thumb position indicator.
                 → ScrollbarView@0.1    (position, content_length)
  Gauge          Percentage-fill bar (Gauge + LineGauge share).
                 → GaugeView@0.1        (ratio numerator, denominator)
  Sparkline      Inline mini bar-history over a sample window.
                 → SparklineView@0.1    (sample window, min, max)
  BarChart       Labeled vertical bars with tick marks.
                 → BarChartView@0.1     (labels, values)
  Chart          Axis + dataset line/scatter plot (Fixed64
                 scaling, no float).
                 → ChartView@0.1        (axis bounds as Fixed64,
                                        dataset point count)
  Canvas         Arbitrary Fixed64-coordinate shape drawing
                 (Bresenham line/rect/circle, braille grid).
                 → CanvasView@0.1       (bounding box, shape count)
  TextInput      Editable single-line/multi-line field with a
                 cursor (TextInput + TextArea share).
                 → TextInputView@0.1    (buffer text, cursor offset)
  Tree           Recursive expand/collapse hierarchical list.
                 → TreeView@0.1         (visible node count,
                                        expanded-path set)
  Calendar       Integer-date month grid with day markers.
                 → CalendarView@0.1     (year, month, marked days)
  Clear          Blank a Rect region (modal-overlay prep).
                 → (no view — no visible state to report)

`Layout` is not a drawn widget and emits no view record; it is
the constraint splitter every consumer calls before assembling
its widget stack.

.section SEMANTIC_PIPE
postui extends pillar 4 (semantically-queryable terminal) to
every screen a TUI app renders. The contract is a two-line
addition inside each widget's `draw()`:

    <w>_view_pack(spec, state, rec_ptr, rec_cap)
    SemanticRegistry::semantic_send(
      SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_<TAG>, rec_ptr, rec_len)

`SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_<TAG>` is a compile-time `u64` constant per
widget-view schema (currently the four-byte MAGIC in the view
header — BLKV / PGVW / LSVW / TBVW / TABV / SBVW / …; the
constant name is what call sites reference, so a later swap to
a BLAKE3-hashed schema name changes no call site).

Every record follows the shape command_record.pdx established
for the shell: fixed header (`u32 magic + u32 record_len +
fields`) + variable payload + zero-pad to an 8-byte boundary.
Every widget's schema is frozen at `@0.1` for v1;
libpdx-semantic-pipe's already-shipped 4-rule version-tolerance
matrix governs what a later `@0.2` may change without breaking
subscribers.

Subscriber side (a scraper, an agent, another tool downstream):

    let bind : [u64; 3] = uninit
    SemanticRegistry::semantic_binding_init(
      &bind, SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_LSVW, on_list_view)
    // per incoming frame:
    SemanticRegistry::semantic_binding_dispatch(
      &bind, incoming_schema, rec_ptr, rec_len)

The 24-byte Binding record is (schema u64, callback u64,
reserved u64); dispatch is two qword loads, one compare, one
tail-call — no allocator, no runtime registry lookup.

At v1 `semantic_send` returns 0 (OK) as a stub; the kernel
`sys_semantic_send` slot lands on the paideia-os side as a
follow-up (tracked cross-repo). The call-site shape does not
change when the syscall lights up.

.section EXTENSION_POINTS
Adding a widget (the "widget #16" recipe) is four edits, all
localised:

  1. WIDGETSPEC       Add `src/widgets/<name>.pdx`. Export a
                      `<Name>Spec` struct (config the caller
                      passes in) and, if stateful, a
                      `<Name>State` struct (cursor / scroll /
                      selection the caller carries across
                      frames — mirrors Ratatui's own
                      spec/state split).
  2. DRAW             Export `<name>_draw(spec, state, area,
                      buf) -> err`. Write cells into `buf`
                      row-major; consult `Block` if the widget
                      wants chrome; consult `Layout` if it
                      splits its own area.
  3. VIEW-PACK        Export `<name>_view_pack(spec, state,
                      rec_ptr, rec_cap) -> rec_len` that lays a
                      frozen `<Name>View@0.1` record: `u32
                      magic + u32 record_len + fixed-scalar
                      fields describing the widget's state +
                      minimum variable payload (labels, values)
                      + zero-pad to 8-byte`. Freeze the field
                      order; version bumps are `@0.2`, never
                      an in-place layout change.
  4. REGISTER         Add `SEMANTIC_SCHEMA_<TAG>` (the view
                      header's MAGIC as a `u64`) to
                      `src/semantic_registry.pdx`. Add
                      `WK_<NAME>` ordinal to
                      `src/widget_kind.pdx`; add a branch to
                      `widget_draw` that tail-calls
                      `<name>_draw`; bump `WK_COUNT`.

Register the source file in `manifest.pdxproj` under `sources:`
and add a unit smoke under `tests/`. No other module recompiles
except the ones you touched — the closed-enum dispatch cost of
"third-party code cannot add a widget without recompiling
postui" is an explicit trade, consistent with every closed
`KIND_*` ordinal set in this org (kernel cap kinds, syscall
numbers, audit event kinds).

.section NON_GOALS
postui v1 deliberately does not ship:

  - Scalar float arithmetic in widget internals. Chart axes
    and Canvas shapes use `Fixed64` (Q32.32) instead. Tracked
    upstream (paideia-as R89-XREPO scalar f32/f64 codegen);
    non-blocking for v1.
  - A heap allocator. Every widget takes caller-owned buffers
    (`Buffer` cells, view-record scratch, string tables). No
    postui module calls `sys_brk` or `sys_mmap`.
  - Dynamic linking or third-party widget plugins. postui is a
    static library; `WidgetKind` is a closed enum. Adding a
    widget requires an edit to `widget_kind.pdx` — see
    EXTENSION_POINTS.
  - A retained-mode scene graph. Immediate-mode redraw only:
    the caller reassembles its widget stack every frame,
    `Buffer` diffing keeps the wire cost proportional to what
    changed, not to what is on screen. A retained-mode GUI
    toolkit is the eventual G4+ Vello/compositor track
    (paideia-os milestones `g1`–`g12`) and is out of scope
    here — postui is terminal-only.
  - Palette / indexed / xterm-256 colour modes. 24-bit
    truecolor throughout. The KIND_TUI_CANVAS cell format is
    truecolor; a terminal that cannot render truecolor is a
    downstream conversion problem.
  - Cassowary or any general linear-constraint solver. Layout
    is a single-pass integer largest-remainder apportionment
    with clamp-and-redistribute (design §2.4) — a total,
    terminating, deterministic function that never reports
    infeasibility.
  - Grapheme-cluster segmentation (UAX #29). Column widths use
    the East-Asian-Width table (UAX #11) via the `Width`
    module; combining marks past v1 land alongside a stdlib
    grapheme routine when one exists.
  - GPU / framebuffer / Kitty-graphics rendering. Cells only,
    KIND_TUI_CANVAS → KIND_TTY. Pixel-plane substrates are
    the G4+ track's problem.

